# Keep the build context minimal and correct.
#
# node_modules MUST be ignored: copying the host's modules into the image would
# defeat the entire point of P5-1, which is to prove the judge's `npm install`
# works from nothing. Without this, `docker build` would silently ship the
# warmed host tree and a broken lockfile would never surface.

node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.data/

# Built by the builder stage from source in the image.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local tooling and agent caches — never part of a shipped app.
.token-optimizer/
.token-optimiser/
.opencode/
.orchestrator/

# Git metadata: not needed to build, and it busts the cache on every commit.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Secrets. .env.example is kept: it is documentation, and it holds no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Evidence and docs are not needed to RUN the app, but the README is the
# submission's front door, so it stays. specs/ and tests/ are excluded to keep
# the context small; neither is needed at runtime.
tests/
specs/